	The katana does higher average damage against the set of all
monsters.

	The katana does 1d10 damage against small monsters, averaging
5.5 points across the board, before enchantment, strength, skill, etc.,
bonuses, which can be dismissed because, except for the small variation
in the maximum skill bonus between classes (and there are more classes
that can get Expert or Skilled in katana... anyone can get Basic in
either, given a little work at it), they'll be the same for either
weapon type.

	The silver saber does 1d8 damage against both small and large,
averaging 4.5 points against most monsters, but gets a 1d20 bonus
(average 10.5 points) against silver-hating monsters. Analysis of my
ascension dumps shows me that silver-haters run about 7% of all monsters
generated (this number is probably actually lower for most people... I
typically spend a lot of time exploring Gehennom the hard way, and most
of the silver-hating monsters aren't normally generated outside
Gehennom). This gives us an average damage of about 5.235 points against
all monsters, inferior to the katana's 5.5.

	And this is even ignoring the fact that katanas do 1d12 damage
(averaging 6.5 points) against large creatures, which include most of
the monsters that take a lot of damage to put down. Also the katana's +1
to-hit bonus, which is irrelevant when used as a secondary and pretty
meaningless for a mid-to-late-game character, but potentially valuable
in the early game.

